returns ok bool: true = success, false = the position is out of range or the node pool is full
`
  'arr.link-peek-back': `
[n]t.link-peek-back: looks at the tail element without removing it
l link: the linked-list state
returns val ?t: ok = the tail value, nil = the list is empty
`
  'arr.link-peek-front': `
[n]t.link-peek-front: looks at the head element without removing it
l link: the linked-list state
returns val ?t: ok = the head value, nil = the list is empty
`
  'arr.link-pop-back': `
[n]t.link-pop-back: pops the element at the tail of the linked list
l link: the linked-list state
returns val ?t: ok = the popped value, nil = the list is empty
`
  'arr.link-pop-front': `
[n]t.link-pop-front: pops the element at the head of the linked list
l link: the linked-list state
returns val ?t: ok = the popped value, nil = the list is empty
`
  'arr.link-push-back': `
[n]t.link-push-back: inserts an element at the tail of the linked list
l link: the linked-list state
