msg: original message to verify
sig: signature to verify R ‖ S (64 bytes)
ok: 1 = signature valid, 0 = invalid
`
  'ed25519.fe-pow': `
Return base^e (e is a little-endian 32-byte exponent, square-and-multiply)
base: base field element (10 limbs)
e: exponent (32 bytes little-endian)
out: resulting field element base^e (10 limbs)
`
  'ed25519.ge-add': `
R = P + Q (add-2008-hwcd, complete addition for a = -1)
r: output point R = P + Q (40-limb extended coordinates)
p: addend point (40-limb extended coordinates)
q: other addend point (40-limb extended coordinates)
`
  'ed25519.ge-basepoint': `
Return the extended coordinates of the base point B (length 40)
bp: extended coordinates of the base point B (point buffer of length 40)
`
  'ed25519.ge-pack': `
Compress a point to 32 bytes (little-endian encoding of y, top bit is the sign of x)
p: point to compress (40-limb extended coordinates)
out: compressed 32 bytes (little-endian encoding of y, top bit is the sign of x)
`
  'ed25519.ge-scalar-mult': `
R = scalar * P (double-and-add, over bits 254..0)
scalar: []byte (little-endian, length >= 32)
r: output point R = scalar * P (40-limb extended coordinates)
p: base point to multiply (40-limb extended coordinates)
`
  'ed25519.ge-unpack': `
Decompress a point from 32 bytes. Returns ok (1/0) and p (point of length 40)
s: compressed point, 32 bytes (little-endian encoding of y, top bit is the sign of x)
ok: 1 = decompression succeeded (a valid y coordinate), 0 = non-square remainder / invalid
p: decompressed point (40-limb extended coordinates; contents are not guaranteed valid when ok = 0)
`
  'ed25519.is-zero-arr': `
Return 1 if all 32 bytes are 0, otherwise 0
a: 32-byte array to test
z: 1 = all 32 bytes are 0, 0 = some byte is nonzero
`
  'ed25519.pcopy': `
Copy a whole point dst = src (40 limbs)
dst: destination point (40 limbs)
src: source point (40 limbs)
`
  'ed25519.sc-ge-l': `
Compare acc (32 bytes): return 1 when acc >= L, otherwise 0
acc: byte-wise scalar to compare (length 32, little-endian)
ge: 1 = acc >= L (group order), 0 = acc < L
`
  'ed25519.sc-muladd': `
Return (a*b + c) mod L (a, b, c each [32]byte)
a: multiplier scalar (32 bytes little-endian)
b: multiplier scalar (32 bytes little-endian)
c: addend scalar (32 bytes little-endian)
s: resulting scalar (a * b + c) mod L (32 bytes)
`
  'ed25519.sc-reduce': `
Reduce s (little-endian integer, any length) mod L, returning [32]byte
Bit-by-bit long division: acc always stays < L; after acc = acc*2 + bit, subtract L when acc >= L
s: little-endian scalar byte string to reduce (any length)
out: the 32-byte result of s mod L
`
  'ed25519.set-coord': `
Write the 10-limb field element src into point p at offset off
p: target point buffer (40 limbs: X‖Y‖Z‖T, each 10 limbs concatenated)
off: starting limb offset within p to write at
src: field element to write (10 limbs)
`
  'embed.exists': `
embed.exists: check whether an embedded file exists
Same linear path-matching logic as read, but does not take the content.
path str: file path (relative to the embed directory)
yes bool: true = an exactly identical path exists in the embed manifest
`
  'embed.read': `
embed.read: read an embedded file (linear path match, then slice from the blob)
path str: file path (relative to the embed directory, e.g. 'index.html'; may contain path separators)
data ?[]byte: ok = file content (a slice over the blob, not copied), nil = path not present
Note: the return value points into the embed region; do not modify its content.
`
  'env.get': `
