buf: target read buffer (capacity must be ≥ n)
n: maximum bytes to read this round
read-n: bytes actually read in; 0 means EOF or an invalid fd
`
  'io.reader.read-all': `
reads everything into buf (at most size bytes)
the caller has to supply the size
buf: the buffer receiving all content (capacity must be ≥ size)
size: the maximum number of bytes allowed to be read in (provided by the caller)
total: bytes actually read in; 0 means EOF or an invalid fd
`
