  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.clear': 'Clears the map'
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.contains': `
Reports whether a key exists
Judged by the result of get: only ok counts as existing (err / nil are both false).
key i64: the key to check
found bool: true=present, false=absent
`
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.for-each': `
Iterates over every (key, value) pair in insertion order
walks the whole linked list via next pointers from head to tail, assigning each node to k / v at every step.
This language has no callbacks; when the function returns, k / v stop at the tail node (the last inserted key-value pair).
k i64: the current node's key
v i64: the current node's value
`
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.get': `
Looks up a key and returns ?i64 (nil = not found)
key i64: the key to query
result ?i64: ok=the corresponding value, nil=absent (returns without probing when the table is empty)
`
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.hash': `
Computes the slot index
key i64: the key to hash
idx i64: key's initial probe position within [0, cap) (key & (cap-1))
`
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.init': 'Initialises the hash table'
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.is-empty': `
Whether the map is empty
empty bool: true=size == 0, false=key/value pairs remain
`
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.len': `
Returns the number of elements
n i64: current number of key/value pairs (putting a new key +1, removing successfully −1)
`
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.put': `
Inserts or updates key→value
linear probing finds a slot: when a key with the same name is hit only the value is updated and its linked-list position is kept (not moved to the tail);
A new key is inserted at the linked-list tail. When the table is full and the key is absent, probing loops forever, so the load factor must be controlled.
key i64: the key
val i64: the value to write (a key of the same name is overwritten)
is-new bool: true=a newly inserted key, false=already existed, only the value was updated
`
  'linked-hash-map.linked-hash-map.remove': `
Removes a key
Clear the slot and unlink the node from the doubly linked list, updating head / tail as well.
key i64: the key to delete
removed bool: true=found and deleted, false=key absent
`
