  'log.set-writer': `
switches the output target to the given io.writer (the abstraction over the io interface).
A writer really wraps nothing but an fd, and the only thing std can persist is a scalar, so its fd is what gets stored.
w: the target io.writer (internally only its fd field is kept for persistent storage)
`
