  'net.listener.accept-with-timeout': `
Accept with a timeout
timeout-ms i64: timeout in milliseconds
returns c ?conn: ok = connection, nil = timeout or failure
`
  'net.listener.close': 'Close the listening socket'
  'net.listener.fd-of': 'Get the file descriptor of the listening socket'
  'net.listener.listen': `
Start listening
host: IP address to bind (e.g. '127.0.0.1')
port: port to listen on
returns ok = true on success
ok: true = bound and listening (fd stays -1 on failure)
`
  'net.listener.set-timeout': `
Set the accept timeout
timeout-ms i64: timeout in milliseconds
returns ok bool: true = success
`
  'net.net-accept': `
Accept a TCP connection
Returns the client fd (-1 = failure)
listen-fd: file descriptor of the listening socket
fd: file descriptor of the newly accepted connection (-1 = failure)
`
  'net.net-accept-nb': `
Accept a TCP connection non-blocking (listening socket set to non-blocking)
Returns the client fd: >= 0 = success, -2 = no pending connection (would-block), -1 = failure
listen-fd: file descriptor of the listening socket already set non-blocking
fd: file descriptor of the newly accepted connection (-1 = failure)
`
  'net.net-dial': `
Establish a TCP client connection
Performs socket + connect
Returns the fd (-1 = failure)
host: target IPv4 dotted address
port: target port
fd: connected socket file descriptor (-1 = connect failed)
`
  'net.net-icmp-open': `
Create an ICMP socket
Returns fd fd (-1 = failure)
fd: file descriptor of the ICMP socket (-1 = failure; macOS uses an unprivileged SOCK_DGRAM, Linux uses SOCK_RAW which needs root)
`
  'net.net-listen': `
Create a TCP listening socket
Performs socket + setsockopt(SO_REUSEADDR) + bind + listen
Returns the fd (-1 = failure)
host: IPv4 dotted address to bind (e.g. '0.0.0.0', '127.0.0.1')
port: port to listen on (e.g. 8080)
fd: file descriptor of the listening socket (-1 = bind/listen failed)
`
  'net.net-recv': `
Receive data
Returns bytes actually received (-1 = error, 0 = connection closed)
fd: connected socket file descriptor
buf: receive buffer (str, must be pre-allocated to at least n bytes)
n: maximum bytes to receive in one call
read-n: bytes actually received (-1 = error, 0 = peer closed)
`
  'net.net-send': `
Send data
Returns bytes actually sent (-1 = error)
fd: connected socket file descriptor
data: content to send (its first n bytes are taken)
n: number of bytes to send
written: bytes actually sent (-1 = error)
`
  'net.net-set-recv-timeout': `
Set the socket receive timeout
Returns 0 = success, -1 = error
fd: socket file descriptor to configure
timeout-ms: maximum milliseconds a receive may block (SO_RCVTIMEO)
ok: 0 = success, -1 = failure
`
  'net.net-udp-open': `
Create a UDP socket
