out: the low-32-bit truncated result (high bits discarded, no range check)
`
  'number.i64.to-str': 'i64 to string\n`#{buildin}: the underlying layer uses the native @str_from_i64 (builtin strconv.go registers the ForwardFunc "i64-to-str",\n(the compiler names the native inline path after it). i64 has a native formatter, so it is a direct builtin — no Nolang loop wrapper.\nout: decimal representation (inlined via native @str_from_i64, e.g. -42 → \'-42\')'
