  'path.is-file': `
checks whether the path is a file
yes: true=.p points to a regular file
`
  'path.join': `
⚠️ API consistency: join()/dir() originally only modified in place and returned nothing, while base()/ext()
returned a str, which made `x = p.join(...)` silently yield an empty string. All four methods now RETURN
a str (join/dir still update .p as well, so the existing in-place usage keeps working).
b: the path element appended to the end of .p
out: the complete path string joined after handling leading/trailing slashes (.p also updated in place)
`
  'path.make-dir': `
creates the directory
returns true = success, false = failure
ok: true=directory created successfully, false=failure
`
  'path.remove': `
deletes the file
returns true = success, false = failure
ok: true=file deleted successfully, false=failure
`
  'path.rename': `
renames this path to new-p
returns true = success, false = failure
new-p: target path string after renaming
ok: true=rename succeeded, false=failure
`
  'path.size': `
gets the file size
