`
  'path.split': `
splits the path into a directory and a file name
Modifies .p in place to the directory part and returns the file name
e.g. path{ p: '/a/b/c.txt' }.split() -> .p='/a/b', f='c.txt'
(struct literals must span several lines; the above is shorthand)
f: the file name split off (.p is changed in place to its directory part)
`
  'pbkdf2.pbkdf2-hmac-sha1': `
PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA1
Legacy protocol compatibility only; new designs should use the SHA-256 / SHA-512 variants.
password []byte: password (UTF-8 byte sequence)
salt []byte: salt
iterations i64: iteration count; larger resists brute force, too small is insecure
key-len i64: desired key length in bytes, generated block by block of 20 bytes
returns out []byte: derived key, exactly key-len bytes long
`
  'pbkdf2.pbkdf2-hmac-sha256': `
PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA256
password []byte: password (UTF-8 byte sequence)
salt []byte: salt, at least 16 bytes and unique per account recommended
iterations i64: iteration count; larger resists brute force (100000+ is common), too small is insecure
key-len i64: desired key length in bytes, generated block by block of 32 bytes
returns out []byte: derived key, exactly key-len bytes long
`
  'pbkdf2.pbkdf2-hmac-sha512': `
PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA512
password []byte: password (UTF-8 byte sequence)
salt []byte: salt, at least 16 bytes and unique per account recommended
iterations i64: iteration count; larger resists brute force, too small is insecure
key-len i64: desired key length in bytes, generated block by block of 64 bytes
returns out []byte: derived key, exactly key-len bytes long
`
  'pem.pem-decode': `
parses a PEM-format string (takes only the first BEGIN…END block in the input)
