  'proxy.config.tls-connect': `
Establish a proxied TLS connection using config
First opens a CONNECT tunnel with the receiver's proxy settings, then completes the TLS handshake over the tunnel.
target-host str: TLS server hostname (used for SNI / certificate verification)
target-port i64: TLS service port
returns tc ?tls.conn: ok = TLS connection with handshake done, nil = failure
`
  'proxy.connect': `
Establish a tunnel through an HTTP CONNECT proxy
Connects to the proxy and sends CONNECT target-host:target-port; the handshake completes on a 200 response;
when username is non-empty a Basic authentication header is attached.
proxy-host str: proxy server hostname or IP
proxy-port i64: proxy server port (HTTP proxies commonly 3128 / 8080)
target-host str: target hostname to tunnel to
target-port i64: target service port (e.g. 443 for HTTPS)
username str: Basic auth username; empty string means no auth header
password str: Basic auth password (ignored when username is empty)
returns fd fd: established tunnel socket descriptor, -1 = connect or handshake failure
`
  'proxy.dial': `
Establish a TCP connection through a proxy (convenience function, no auth)
Equivalent to connect(..., '', '').
proxy-host str: proxy server hostname or IP
proxy-port i64: proxy server port
target-host str: target hostname to tunnel to
target-port i64: target service port
returns fd fd: established tunnel socket descriptor, -1 = failure
`
  'proxy.dial-auth': `
Establish a TCP connection through a proxy (with auth)
Same as connect(...) with credentials spelled out as parameters.
proxy-host str: proxy server hostname or IP
proxy-port i64: proxy server port
target-host str: target hostname to tunnel to
target-port i64: target service port
username str: Basic auth username
password str: Basic auth password
returns fd fd: established tunnel socket descriptor, -1 = failure
`
  'proxy.proxy-tls-dial': `
Establish a TLS connection through a proxy
Performs an HTTP CONNECT (without auth) to get a tunnel, then starts the TLS handshake over it.
proxy-host str: proxy server hostname or IP
proxy-port i64: proxy server port
target-host str: TLS server hostname (also used for SNI / certificate verification in the handshake)
target-port i64: TLS service port (usually 443)
returns tc ?tls.conn: ok = TLS connection handshaked over the tunnel, nil = tunnel or handshake failed at any stage
`
  'proxy.socks5-connect': `
Establish a connection through a SOCKS5 proxy
First negotiates methods (0x02 username/password auth when username is non-empty, otherwise 0x00 no auth),
then hands the target address to the proxy with the CONNECT command.
proxy-host str: SOCKS5 proxy hostname or IP
proxy-port i64: SOCKS5 proxy port (usually 1080)
target-host str: target host to tunnel to; non-IP literals are passed to the proxy as a domain name string for it to resolve
target-port i64: target service port
username str: username; empty string means no authentication
password str: password (ignored when username is empty)
returns fd fd: established tunnel socket descriptor, -1 = negotiation or connect failure
`
  'proxy.socks5-dial': `
Establish a connection through a SOCKS5 proxy (convenience function, no auth)
Equivalent to socks5-connect(..., '', ''), using 0x00 no-auth negotiation.
proxy-host str: SOCKS5 proxy hostname or IP
proxy-port i64: SOCKS5 proxy port (usually 1080)
target-host str: target host to tunnel to; non-IP literals are passed to the proxy as a domain name string for it to resolve
target-port i64: target service port
returns fd fd: established tunnel socket descriptor, -1 = failure
`
