  'set.add': `
adds an element to the set (if absent)
val t: the element to add
returns new-size i64: the new size
`
  'set.contains': `
reports whether an element is in the set
val t: the element to look for
returns yes bool: true = present, false = absent
`
  'set.difference': `
computes the difference (in this set but not in other)
the result is written into the caller-supplied out buffer and the number of elements is returned
other []t: the other set's element buffer
osize i64: the other set's element count
out []t: the buffer for the difference
returns cnt i64: the number of elements in the difference
`
  'set.init': `
factory — builds an empty set on a caller-supplied element buffer
data []t: the element buffer (its length is the capacity ceiling)
returns s set: the initialised set instance
`
  'set.intersection': `
computes the intersection (elements in both this set and other)
the result is written into the caller-supplied out buffer and the number of elements is returned
other []t: the other set's element buffer
osize i64: the other set's element count
out []t: the buffer for the intersection
returns cnt i64: the number of elements in the intersection
`
  'set.is-empty': `
reports whether the set is empty
yes: true when the collection holds no elements
`
  'set.remove': `
removes an element from the set
fills the hole with the last element (so order is not preserved)
val t: the element to remove
returns new-size i64: the new size
`
  'set.size': `
returns the set size
sz: number of elements currently held by the set
`
  'set.to-vec': `
converts the set to a slice (unordered)
returns out []t: the slice of elements (length = size)
`
  'set.union': `
computes the union (adds the elements of other's buffer that this set lacks)
other []t: the other set's element buffer
osize i64: the other set's element count
returns new-size i64: the size after the union
`
  'sha1.sha1': `
Compute the SHA-1 hash (padding and multi-block handling included)
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hash [20]byte: 160-bit digest stored big-endian as defined by FIPS 180-4
Note: SHA-1 no longer offers collision resistance; use it only for legacy protocol compatibility / checksums
`
  'sha1.sha1-block': `
Process one 512-bit block (80-round compression, FIPS 180-4)
s []u32: 16 32-bit big-endian message words (already unpacked from bytes by the caller)
h0 u32, h1 u32, h2 u32, h3 u32, h4 u32: the 160-bit hash state entering this block
r0 u32, r1 u32, r2 u32, r3 u32, r4 u32: the new state after compression (working variables added back to the input state modulo 2^32)
`
  'sha1.sha1-hex': `
Compute the SHA-1 hash and return a hex string
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hex str: 40-character lowercase hexadecimal digest
`
  'sha224.sha224': `
Compute the SHA-224 hash (padding and multi-block handling included; same compression function as SHA-256, different initial values)
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hash [28]byte: 224-bit digest (the first 7 SHA-256 state words), stored big-endian
`
  'sha224.sha224-hex': `
Compute the SHA-224 hash and return a hex string
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hex str: 56-character lowercase hexadecimal digest
`
  'sha256.sha256': `
Compute the SHA-256 hash (padding and multi-block handling included)
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hash [32]byte: 256-bit digest stored big-endian as defined by FIPS 180-4
`
  'sha256.sha256-block': `
Process one 512-bit block (64-round compression, FIPS 180-4)
s []u32: 16 32-bit big-endian message words (already unpacked from bytes by the caller)
h0 u32..h7 u32: the 256-bit hash state entering this block (initial values of a..h)
r0 u32..r7 u32: the new state after compression (working variables added back to the input state modulo 2^32)
`
  'sha256.sha256-hex': `
Compute the SHA-256 hash and return a hex string
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hex str: 64-character lowercase hexadecimal digest
`
  'sha3.keccak-f1600': `
Run the Keccak-f[1600] permutation (24 rounds)
state: state array of 25 64-bit lanes (in-place input/output)
`
  'sha3.keccak-sponge': `
Keccak sponge function
data []byte: raw bytes to absorb into the sponge state, may be empty
rate: absorption rate in bytes (must be a multiple of 8)
capacity: capacity in bytes (rate + capacity = 200)
out-len: desired output length in bytes
suffix: padding suffix (SHA-3 = 0x06, SHAKE = 0x1F)
returns out []byte: the squeezed hash/output bytes
`
  'sha3.rotl64': `
64-bit rotate left
x: 64-bit value to rotate left
n: rotation amount (0..63, taken mod 64 first to avoid the undefined behavior of shifting by 64)
r: result after rotating left
`
  'sha3.sha3-224': `
Compute the SHA3-224 hash
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hash [28]byte: 28-byte hash value
`
  'sha3.sha3-224-hex': `
Compute SHA3-224 and return a hex string
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hex str: 56-character hex string
`
  'sha3.sha3-256': `
Compute the SHA3-256 hash
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hash [32]byte: 32-byte hash value
`
  'sha3.sha3-256-hex': `
Compute SHA3-256 and return a hex string
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hex str: 64-character hex string
`
  'sha3.sha3-384': `
Compute the SHA3-384 hash
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hash [48]byte: 48-byte hash value
`
  'sha3.sha3-384-hex': `
Compute SHA3-384 and return a hex string
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hex str: 96-character hex string
`
  'sha3.sha3-512': `
Compute the SHA3-512 hash
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hash [64]byte: 64-byte hash value
`
  'sha3.sha3-512-hex': `
Compute SHA3-512 and return a hex string
data []byte: raw bytes to hash, may be empty
returns hex str: 128-character hex string
`
  'sha384.sha384': `
Compute the SHA-384 hash (padding and multi-block handling included; same compression function as SHA-512, different initial values)
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hash [48]byte: 384-bit digest (the first 6 SHA-512 state words), stored big-endian
`
  'sha384.sha384-hex': `
Compute the SHA-384 hash and return a hex string
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hex str: 96-character lowercase hexadecimal digest
`
  'sha512.sha512': `
Compute the SHA-512 hash (padding and multi-block handling included)
data []byte: input byte array (any length; message length limit 2^128-1 bits)
hash [64]byte: 512-bit digest stored big-endian as defined by FIPS 180-4
`
  'sha512.sha512-block': `
Process one 1024-bit block (80-round compression, FIPS 180-4)
s []u64: 16 64-bit big-endian message words (already unpacked from bytes by the caller)
h0 u64..h7 u64: the 512-bit hash state entering this block (initial values of a..h)
r0 u64..r7 u64: the new state after compression (working variables added back to the input state modulo 2^64)
`
  'sha512.sha512-hex': `
Compute the SHA-512 hash and return a hex string
data []byte: input byte array (any length)
hex str: 128-character lowercase hexadecimal digest
`
