returns client ?client:
ok = connected client
nil   = connection failed
err = error message
`
  'stack.stack.clear': `
Clear the stack (set n to 0; data is not freed and old contents are not erased)
No parameters and no return value; size() is 0 after clearing
`
  'stack.stack.empty': `
Reports whether the stack is empty
yes bool: true means n == 0
`
  'stack.stack.peek': `
Peeks at the top element without removing it
val ?i64: ok=data[n-1], nil=the stack is empty
`
  'stack.stack.pop': `
Pops an element from the top of the stack
val ?i64: ok=the original top element (removed), nil=the stack is empty
`
  'stack.stack.push': `
Pushes an element onto the top of the stack
Note: this method does not check capacity; the caller must guarantee n < len(data).
val i64: the value to push; written to data[n] then n increments by 1
`
  'stack.stack.size': `
returns the current element count of the stack
sz i64: equals n (0 means empty, at most len(data))
`
