  'str.set-byte': `
Returns ?bool (may fail): out of range (i < 0 or i >= the entity's capacity cap) returns nil and **skips the write**,
On success returns some(true). The bound uses %str-long's cap (entity capacity) rather than len, so "fill the buffer first,
the "then set len" build program still works as before. Callers may legally discard the ?bool with a bare statement (optunuse only tracks binding names).
