  'tls.conn.decrypt-record': `
Decrypt a record
buf []byte: received record data (starting from the header)
returns ct i64: original content type (-1 = error)
returns out []byte: decrypted plaintext
expected-ct i64: expected content type (compared after decryption; a mismatch counts as an error)
`
  'tls.conn.decrypt-record-13': `
TLS 1.3 AEAD record decryption
rec []byte: received record (with header)
key [16]byte: AEAD key
iv [12]byte: AEAD IV
seq i64: expected sequence number of this record (participates in nonce derivation; a wrong order fails AEAD verification)
returns ct i64: original content type (-1 = error)
returns out []byte: decrypted plaintext (excluding the content type byte)
`
  'tls.conn.decrypt-record-gcm': `
TLS 1.2 AES-128-GCM AEAD record decryption (RFC 5288)
buf []byte: received record (starting from the header)
expected-ct i64: expected content type (used as AAD)
key [16]byte: server_write_key
salt [4]byte: server_write_IV (implicit salt)
seq i64: record sequence number
returns ct i64: success = expected-ct, -1 = error
returns out []byte: decrypted plaintext
`
  'tls.conn.derive-application-keys-13': 'Derive the application keys'
  'tls.conn.derive-handshake-keys-13': `
derive-traffic-keys-13: derive handshake keys and application keys
Using the HKDF key schedule (RFC 8446 §7.1)
`
  'tls.conn.derive-keys': `
Derive all keys from the premaster secret
premaster []byte: premaster secret (static-RSA 48 bytes / ECDHE 32 bytes)
