`
  'txt.split-n': `
splitting with a bounded count
sep txt, maxsplit i64: the maximum number of splits (<=0 means unlimited)
sep: the separator txt
maxsplit: maximum number of splits (<= 0 means unlimited)
out: slice of split results (at most maxsplit+1 parts)
`
  'txt.starts-with': `
Whether it starts with the given prefix
sub: the prefix sub-txt
yes: whether it starts with sub
`
  'txt.to-bigint': `
parses the text into a bigint, detecting the base automatically
Prefixes 0b/0B -> binary, 0o/0O -> octal, 0x/0X -> hexadecimal; no prefix -> decimal
Accepts optional leading whitespace and a sign (+ / -)
returns ?bigint: ok(bigint) on success / nil for an empty string / err('msg') when there are no digits
out: ok=a bigint parsed with the prefix radix (0b/0o/0x or decimal), nil=empty, err=no valid digits
`
  'txt.to-bool': `
parses "true"/"false" into a bool
