AlgorithmIdentifier for rsaEncryption (1.2.840.113549.1.1.1)
returns out []byte: SEQUENCE { OID rsaEncryption, NULL }
`
  'x509.alg-id-sha256-with-rsa': `
AlgorithmIdentifier for sha256WithRSAEncryption (1.2.840.113549.1.1.11)
returns out []byte: SEQUENCE { OID sha256WithRSAEncryption, NULL }
`
  'x509.der-enc-bitstring': `
Wrap as a BIT STRING
data []byte: byte data
returns out []byte: DER BIT STRING
data: bit string content (byte aligned; the function prepends the unused-bits-count byte 0 automatically)
out: DER BIT STRING with tag=0x03 (content one byte longer than data)
`
  'x509.der-enc-explicit': `
EXPLICIT context tag [n]
tag-num i64: tag number (0, 1, 2, ...); the low 5 bits are combined with 0xA0 to form the tag
content []byte: inner DER encoding to wrap in this context tag
returns out []byte: DER [n] EXPLICIT (constructed tag + length + content)
`
  'x509.der-enc-integer-bytes': `
Encode a big-endian byte array as a DER INTEGER
data []byte: big-endian bytes (positive integer)
returns out []byte: DER INTEGER (with tag+length)
`
  'x509.der-enc-integer-i64': `
Encode an i64 as a DER INTEGER
val i64: integer value
returns out []byte: DER INTEGER
`
  'x509.der-enc-len': `
Encode a DER length
val i64: length value
returns out []byte: DER length bytes
`
  'x509.der-enc-null': `
Encode DER NULL (content always empty)
out: the two bytes 05 00
`
  'x509.der-enc-octetstring': `
Wrap as an OCTET STRING
data: raw bytes to embed (algorithm parameters, digests, etc.)
out: DER OCTET STRING with tag=0x04
`
  'x509.der-enc-oid-raw': `
Encode from raw OID content bytes (without tag+length)
raw []byte: OID content bytes (e.g. rsaEncryption = [0x2A, 0x86, 0x48, ...])
returns out []byte: DER OBJECT IDENTIFIER (with tag+length)
`
  'x509.der-enc-printablestring': `
Encode a DER PrintableString (taking the string's bytes verbatim as content)
s: text to encode (the caller must guarantee printable ASCII within the PrintableString character set)
out: DER TLV with tag=0x13
`
  'x509.der-enc-sequence': `
Wrap as a SEQUENCE
content: DER encodings of the child nodes concatenated in order (each already with its tag+length)
out: DER SEQUENCE with tag=0x30
`
  'x509.der-enc-set': `
Wrap as a SET
content: DER encodings of the member nodes concatenated
out: DER SET with tag=0x31
`
  'x509.der-enc-tlv': `
Wrap a TLV
tag i64: tag byte (e.g. 0x02 INTEGER, 0x17 UTCTime)
content []byte: content bytes to wrap (may be empty; the length field is still written when length is 0)
returns out []byte: complete TLV (tag + DER length + content)
`
  'x509.der-enc-utctime': `
Encode a DER UTCTime
s: time text in the form YYMMDDHHMMSSZ (e.g. "240101000000Z")
out: DER TLV with tag=0x17
`
  'x509.der-len': `
Decode a DER length
data []byte: DER-encoded data
pos i64: offset where the length bytes start (1 byte for the short form; in the long form the low 7 bits of the first byte say how many following bytes encode the length)
len i64: output length value
adv i64: number of bytes consumed by the length field itself (1 for the short form, 1 + number-of-length-bytes for the long form; callers skip to the value with pos+adv)
`
  'x509.der-skip': `
Skip one DER TLV element
data: DER encoded data
pos: current position (pointing at the tag byte)
next: output position of the next element
`
  'x509.der-tag': `
Read the DER tag byte
data: DER encoded data, pos: position
tag: output tag value
pos: offset of the tag byte (only data[pos] is read, no advance; the caller moves past it)
`
  'x509.rsa-pkcs1-sign-sha256': `
Sign data with RSA PKCS#1 v1.5
data []byte: data to sign
n []byte: modulus (big-endian)
d []byte: private exponent (big-endian)
returns sig []byte: signature (modulus length)
`
  'x509.sha256-compress': `
SHA-256 single-block compression
Runs 64 rounds over the 16 32-bit message words and adds the result back onto the input state.
w0..w15 i64: the 16 32-bit big-endian words of the current 512-bit block (only the low 32 bits of each word are used)
hin0..hin7 i64: the 8 32-bit hash state words entering this block (initial values of a..h)
h0..h7 i64: the 8 32-bit state words after compression (hin + working variables, already & 0xFFFFFFFF)
`
