`
  'x509.x509-bytes-to-bn': `
big-endian byte array → []i64 (little-endian base 2^32)
Local copy to avoid a circular dependency with net/tls.no
data []byte: big-endian bytes
returns out []i64: big integer (each element a 32-bit limb)
`
  'x509.x509-fingerprint': `
x509-fingerprint: compute the SHA-256 fingerprint of an X.509 certificate
That is the SHA-256 hash of the certificate's TBSCertificate substructure (not of the whole DER).
First locates the TBSCertificate bytes with x509-tbs-range, feeds them to sha256.sha256,
then combines the 32-byte hash into 8 big-endian 32-bit words for the return.
data: the certificate's full DER bytes
h0 i64: highest 32-bit word of the fingerprint (big-endian, 0 when the TBSCertificate cannot be located)
h1 i64: the 2nd 32-bit word in descending order
h2 i64: the 3rd 32-bit word in descending order
h3 i64: the 4th 32-bit word in descending order
h4 i64: the 5th 32-bit word in descending order
h5 i64: the 6th 32-bit word in descending order
h6 i64: the 7th 32-bit word in descending order
h7 i64: the lowest 32-bit word (all zeros mean the certificate has no parsable TBSCertificate)
`
  'x509.x509-rsa-e': `
Extract the RSA public exponent (usually 65537)
data: DER encoded certificate
e: output exponent value (0 = not RSA or parse failure)
`
  'x509.x509-rsa-n': `
Extract the RSA public modulus (big-endian byte array)
data []byte: DER encoded certificate
returns out []byte: modulus bytes (big-endian, without a leading 0x00)
`
  'x509.x509-serial': `
Extract the certificate serial number (when it fits in an i64)
data: DER encoded certificate
serial: output serial number (0 = cannot extract)
`
  'x509.x509-tbs-range': `
Find the byte range of the TBSCertificate
data: DER encoded certificate
start: output TBS start position (including the SEQUENCE tag)
end: output TBS end position (exclusive, i.e. the start of the next element)
`
  'xz.lzma-decoder.decode': `
LZMA decoding main loop
data: compressed data, start-pos: data start position
unpacked-size: expected decompressed size (-1 = unknown)
start-pos: offset in data where LZMA stream decoding begins
`
  'xz.lzma-decoder.decode-distance': `
Decode a match distance
length: match length (used to pick the distance encoding)
dist: match distance (byte offset back from the current write position)
`
  'xz.lzma-decoder.decode-length': `
Decode a match length
probs: probability array, returns the length
length: decoded match length (combining selector and low/aligned bits)
`
  'xz.lzma-decoder.decode-literal': 'Decode a literal'
  'xz.lzma-decoder.init-probs': 'Initialize all probabilities to 0x400 (even chance)'
  'xz.lzma-decoder.update-state-literal': 'Update the state (after a literal)'
  'xz.lzma-decoder.update-state-match': 'Update the state (after a match)'
  'xz.lzma-decoder.update-state-rep': 'Update the state (after a repeat match)'
  'xz.lzma-decoder.update-state-shortrep': 'Update the state (after a short repeat)'
  'xz.lzma-decompress': `
.lzma format:
- 1 byte: properties (lc, lp, pb encoding)
- 4 bytes: dict size (little-endian)
- 8 bytes: unpacked size (little-endian, 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF = unknown)
- compressed data
`
  'xz.lzma-rd.decode-bit': `
Decode one bit
prob: probability value (0-0x7FFF), returns the bit and the updated prob
bit: decoded bit (0 or 1)
new-prob: adaptively updated probability value (for the next decode)
`
  'xz.lzma-rd.decode-bit-tree': `
Decode a bit tree
num-bits: tree depth, probs: probability array, returns the symbol
probs: probability array of the bit tree nodes
sym: symbol value decoded by walking the tree bit by bit to the leaf
`
  'xz.lzma-rd.decode-direct-bits': `
Decode n direct bits
num-bits: number of direct bits to decode (bypassing the probability model)
res: raw integer value assembled from num-bits bits
`
  'xz.lzma-rd.decode-reverse-bit-tree': `
Decode a reverse bit tree
probs: probability array of the bit tree nodes
num-bits: tree depth (bits of the decoded symbol)
sym: symbol value decoded walking the tree in reverse (low bit to high bit)
`
  'xz.lzma-rd.init': `
Initialize the range decoder
data: LZMA compressed byte stream to decode
start-pos: byte offset in data where decoding starts
`
  'xz.lzma-rd.normalize': 'Range decoder normalization'
  'xz.lzma2-decompress-stream': `
Decompress an LZMA2 stream
LZMA2 uses control bytes to split chunks:
0x00 = end
0x01 = uncompressed with dictionary reset (with 4-byte dictionary id)
0x02 = uncompressed without dictionary reset
0x80-0xBF = LZMA compressed (possibly with dictionary reset)
out is a named result parameter (out-parameter syntax sugar): the call site binds the receiving variable on the LHS.
The body accumulates into a local res first and delivers out = res at the end (the same pattern as
inflate-decompress in gzip.no); declaring out as an ordinary input parameter would make it a read-only
reference, so pushed results could never reach the caller.
data: the LZMA2 stream including control bytes
start-pos: starting offset of the stream
out: decompressed plaintext byte stream (named output parameter, delivered once at the end)
`
  'xz.xz-compress': `
Compress data in xz format (basic implementation)
data: raw data ([]byte)
out: xz-compressed data ([]byte)
Note: currently a basic implementation using stored blocks;
full LZMA2 compression is left for a later implementation.
`
  'xz.xz-decompress': `
.xz format:
- Stream Header: 6 bytes magic + 2 bytes stream flags
- Blocks: Block Header + Compressed Data + Block Padding + Check
- Index
- Stream Footer: 12 bytes
`
