  'yaml.scalar-text': `
The scalar text of the current node (containers return ok=false)
out: scalar text (nil=container node)
`
  'yaml.source-of': `
The original input text
out: the original input text at parse time
`
  'yaml.str': `
Get the string value (numbers/booleans return their raw text)
val: the scalar raw text (nil=container node)
`
  'yaml.stringify': `
Alias for to-yaml
out: same output as to-yaml
`
  'yaml.strip-bom': `
Strip a leading UTF-8 BOM
s: text that may carry a BOM
out: text with the leading EF BB BF removed
`
  'yaml.style': `
The style of the current node
s: that node's YAML-STYLE-* style constant
`
  'yaml.tag': `
The explicit tag of the current node
t: the node's explicit tag (empty string=none)
`
  'yaml.text': `
The scalar raw text of the current node
t: scalar raw text (empty string for container nodes)
`
  'yaml.to-json': `
Convert the current document to JSON
out: JSON text of the current document's root node
`
  'yaml.to-json-all': `
Convert all documents into a JSON array
out: JSON array text of all documents
`
  'yaml.to-yaml': `
Re-output the current document as YAML
out: YAML text of the current document re-emitted
`
  'yaml.valid': `
Whether this document parsed successfully (getting a yaml value means success)
yes: the handle carries a successfully parsed document
`
  'yaml.valid-of': `
Whether the source text can be parsed (without building a document)
source: the YAML source text to validate
yes: the source text can be parsed
`
  'yaml.value': `
Get the value node of the i-th key of a mapping
i: key/value pair ordinal (0-based)
out: value node of the i-th key pair (nil=out of range or not a mapping)
`
  'yaml.yaml-apply-tag': `
Decide the node type by the explicit tag
tag: the normalized tag name
kind: node kind inferred from the content
k: final kind after label override (original kind returned when the label is unrecognized)
`
  'yaml.yaml-emit': `
emits a node as block-style YAML (no trailing newline)
pool: the node pool
idx: index of the node to emit
indent: number of spaces per indent level
depth: the current nesting depth
out: block-style YAML text (no trailing newline)
`
  'yaml.yaml-f-is-inf': `
Does not use literal comparison: Nolang numeric literals do not support exponents (`1e308` is cut into `1` + `e308`).
The test for infinity is "nonzero and unchanged after halving"; NaN is excluded first with `x != x`.
x: the f64 value to test
yes: x is positive/negative infinity (nonzero and unchanged after halving)
`
  'yaml.yaml-f-is-nan': `
Whether the float is NaN (NaN != NaN)
Does not use `float.is-nan`: receiver-style calls inside the module cannot resolve that method in the MIR backend.
x: the f64 value to test
yes: x is NaN (the NaN != NaN test)
`
  'yaml.yaml-hex-char': `
Convert a single hex digit (0-15) to a character
v: the numeric value of a hex digit, 0-15
ch: the corresponding hex character ('0'-'f')
`
  'yaml.yaml-hex-digit': `
Convert a hex character to its value; non-hex returns -1
c: the ASCII code of the character
d: the value 0-15 represented by this hex digit (-1=invalid hex character)
`
  'yaml.yaml-inf': `
Positive infinity
v: positive infinity
`
  'yaml.yaml-json-escape': `
JSON string escaping
s: the raw string
out: escaped JSON string (with enclosing double quotes)
`
  'yaml.yaml-json-of': `
converts a node to JSON
pool: the node pool
idx: index of the node to convert
depth: remaining recursion depth (prevents alias cycles)
out: the JSON text corresponding to that node
`
  'yaml.yaml-key-eq': `
Whether two key nodes are equivalent (compares scalar text)
a: key node a
b: key node b
yes: the two nodes' scalar texts are equal
`
  'yaml.yaml-key-text-eq': `
Whether the scalar key text equals the given string
nd: the node to compare (its scalar text is taken)
key: the target text
yes: nd's scalar text equals key
`
  'yaml.yaml-nan': `
Must go through runtime division: compile-time constant folding computes `0.0 / 0.0` directly as 0.
Routing through a local variable avoids folding and yields a real NaN (`x != x` is true).
v: the NaN value (produced at runtime by 0.0/0.0, not constant-folded)
`
  'yaml.yaml-node-is-nan': '`.nan`\'s fval is filled with a real NaN by yaml-nan(), so it is compared by value (NaN != NaN).\nnode raw-text check as fallback: paths like tag rewriting may change only text without recomputing fval.\nnd: the node to inspect\nyes: the node is .nan'
  'yaml.yaml-parse-radix': `
parses a radix-base integer (underscores ignored)
t: text containing digits
start: start offset of the number
radix: radix base (2/8/16)
kind: success=YAML-KIND-INT, failure=YAML-KIND-STR
v: the integer value converted out
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.advance': 'Advance one byte'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.anchor-id': `
Search for an anchor; returns -1 if not found
name: anchor name
idx: the corresponding node index (-1=not registered)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.at': `
The byte offset k relative to the current position
k: offset relative to the current position (out-of-range reads yield 0)
c: the byte value at pos+k
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.at-doc-marker': `
Whether the current position is --- (1) or ... (2)
which: 1='---', 2='...', 0=not a document marker
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.at-eol': `
Whether it is at the end of the line (EOF included)
yes: the current byte is \n or the end of input has been reached
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.byte-at': `
Returns src[i], or 0 when out of range
i: the target index
c: the byte value at that position (0 when out of range)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.cur': `
The current byte
c: the byte currently at pos (0 at EOF)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.eof': `
Whether the end of the input has been reached
yes: pos has reached the end of the input
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.fail': `
records a parse error
msg: error description (stored into the parser's error message)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.fail-at': `
records a parse error with position
msg: error description (current position info appended automatically)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.indent-at': `
Skips leading spaces before counting: call sites almost always follow skip-blank-lines() directly,
Here pos stops at the line start (column 0), so subtracting directly always yields 0, making nested blocks judged as "not indented".
after skipping, pos stops at the first non-space character; the later is-seq-dash / looks-like-map-entry /
at-doc-marker also needs this position.
ind: number of spaces before the first non-space character on the current line
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.is-seq-dash': `
Whether the current position is the sequence-item indicator '- '
yes: the current position is a sequence-item indicator ('- ' or a '-' at end of line)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.line-end-of': `
returns the end-of-line offset of the line containing i (pointing at the newline or n)
i: any byte offset within the target line
le: end-of-line offset (points at the newline; equals the input length when there is none)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.line-start-of': `
Returns the start offset of the line containing i
i: any byte offset within the target line
ls: byte offset of the start of the line containing i
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.looks-like-map-entry': `
Whether this line has a top-level ': ', a trailing ':', or an explicit key '? '
yes: this line has a mapping-key indicator and can be treated as a mapping entry
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.merge-into': `
Merge handling of key << (supports mappings or sequences of mappings)
keys: list of key node indices of the target mapping
vals: the list of value-node indices of the target mapping
src: value node index of the merge key (<<) (a MAP or a MAP sequence)
ok-keys: merged key list
ok-vals: merged value list
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.merge-one': `
Merge one mapping's entries into keys/vals (existing keys are not overwritten)
note: the MIR backend does not allow moving an input vec directly into another vec (borrow/ownership protection),
So this copies element by element rather than ok-keys = keys.
keys: list of key node indices of the target mapping
vals: the list of value-node indices of the target mapping
src: index of the mapping node to merge (must be of kind MAP)
ok-keys: merged key list (existing keys are kept first)
ok-vals: merged value list
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.newline': `
Consume one newline (\n or \r\n)
yes: consumed one newline; false=not at a newline, position unchanged
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-alias': `
Parses the alias *name
idx: node index the alias points to (-1=anchor absent, error already recorded)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block': `
parses one block-context node (the current position is the node's start column)
indent: the node's starting column
cont-min: the minimum continuation indent passed to child nodes
idx: pool index of the parsed node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-indented': `
parses deeper-indented following lines as the value
parent-indent: indentation column of the parent key line (later lines must be deeper to count as values)
idx: pool index of the parsed value node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-map': `
parses a block mapping
indent: the indent column of the mapping key (basis for same-level keys and dedent decisions)
idx: pool index of the new mapping node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-scalar': `
parses block scalars | and >
cont-min: the indent column the block content must reach (passed in by the calling context)
idx: pool index of the new block-scalar node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-block-seq': `
parses a block sequence
indent: the indent column of the sequence item '-' (basis for sibling and dedent decisions)
idx: pool index of the new sequence node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-docs': `
parses all documents
roots: pool index list of each document's root node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-document': `
parses one document and returns the root node index
idx: pool index of this document's root node (-1=parse failure)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-double': `
parses a double-quoted scalar
idx: pool index of the new scalar node (escapes already processed)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-flow-map': `
Parses {k: v, ...}
idx: pool index of the new mapping node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-flow-node': `
parses one flow-context node
cont-min: the minimum continuation indent passed to nested scalar parsing
key-mode: true=parse at a key position
flow: true=flow context
idx: pool index of the parsed node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-flow-seq': `
Parses [a, b, ...]
idx: pool index of the new sequence node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-plain': `
parses a plain scalar (multi-line folding included)
cont-min: the minimum indent column required for multi-line folded continuations (0=no cross-line continuation)
key-mode: true=parse as a mapping key, terminating at indicators such as ': '
flow: true=flow context (',' '}' ']' also terminate)
idx: pool index of the new scalar node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-props': `
parses the node-prefix anchor and tag (in either order)
tag: the tag read (empty string=none)
anchor: the anchor name read (empty = none; non-empty means it has been registered in the anchor table)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.parse-single': `
parses a single-quoted scalar
idx: pool index of the new scalar node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.push-node': `
appends a node and returns its index
nd: the node to append
idx: the node's index in the node pool
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.push-null': `
appends an empty node (null)
idx: pool index of the new null node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.push-scalar': `
Builds a scalar node from the style and the tag
text: scalar text
style: scalar style (YAML-STYLE-* constants)
tag: explicit tag (empty=type inferred by the core schema)
anchor: anchor name (empty = none)
idx: pool index of the new node
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.read-line-content': `
reads from the current position to the end of line (trailing whitespace and comments stripped)
out: text up to the end of line (trailing whitespace and # comments removed)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.read-tag': `
reads a tag (!!name / !name / !<verbatim> / !)
out: full tag text (with the ! prefix; a bare ! returns ';!')
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.read-token': `
reads a bare token containing no delimiters
out: the bare token read (terminates at whitespace/indicators)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.register-anchor': `
Register an anchor
name: anchor name
idx: the node index the anchor points to
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.set-props': `
Attach a tag and an anchor to a node (and register the anchor)
idx: the target node-pool index
tag: explicit tag (empty string=none)
anchor: anchor name (empty = none; non-empty is registered too)
`
  'yaml.yaml-parser.skip-blank-lines': 'skips blank lines and full-line comments, stopping at the start of the next content line'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.skip-doc-preamble': 'skips blank lines, comments, and directive lines'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.skip-flow-ws': 'Whitespace inside flow contexts — in-line spaces, newlines and comments'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.skip-spaces': 'skips inline spaces and tabs'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.skip-to-doc-boundary': 'skips the rest of the current document, stopping at the next --- or end of input'
  'yaml.yaml-parser.skip-to-eol': 'skips trailing whitespace and line comments (does not consume the newline)'
  'yaml.yaml-plain-safe': `
Whether the text can be output as-is as a plain scalar
s: the text to output
yes: can be output as-is as a plain scalar (no quoting needed)
`
  'yaml.yaml-quote': `
emits a double-quoted YAML scalar
s: the raw text
out: YAML scalar text wrapped in double quotes and escaped
`
  'yaml.yaml-resolve-plain': `
Infer the plain scalar type by the core schema
text: the plain scalar raw text
kind: inferred node kind (null/bool/int/float/str etc.)
ival: the integer value when kind=INT
fval: the floating-point value when kind=FLOAT
bval: the boolean value when kind=BOOL
`
  'yaml.yaml-scalar-repr': `
The YAML representation of the scalar
nd: scalar node
out: the YAML representation text chosen by kind and style
`
  'yaml.yaml-scan-number': `
Try to parse the text as an integer or a float
returns kind = YAML-KIND-INT / YAML-KIND-FLOAT / YAML-KIND-STR (not a number)
t: scalar text
kind: recognized number kind (INT/FLOAT/STR)
ival: the integer value when kind=INT
fval: the floating-point value when kind=FLOAT
`
  'yaml.yaml-spaces': `
Generate n spaces
n: number of spaces
out: a string of n spaces
`
  'yaml.yaml-str-at': `
Why this helper is needed: `arr[i]` (arr being []str) returns option<str> by default,
while the MIR backend emits invalid IR when option<str> is used as a call argument / method receiver
(%option_str does not match %str-long). String concatenation auto-unwraps the option,
So here `out = out - a[i]` takes the element, which both unpacks and satisfies `no vet`'s out-of-bounds check.
a: target string array
i: element index
out: value of the i-th element (empty string when out of range)
`
  'yaml.yaml-tag-name': `
Normalize a tag name (!!str / tag:yaml.org,2002:str → str)
tag: the raw tag (spellings like !!str / tag:yaml.org,2002:str)
name: normalized short tag name (str/int/seq...)
`
  'yaml.yaml-to-f64': `
Convert text to f64 (returning nil means failure)
t: digit text
v: the conversion result (nil=cannot be parsed as f64)
`
  'yaml.yaml-to-i64': `
Convert text to i64; returns -1 on failure
s: integer text
v: the converted value (-1=conversion failed)
`
  'yaml.yaml-unescape-double': `
handles double-quote escape sequences
body: the string content inside double quotes (escape sequences included)
out: unescaped text (nil=contains illegal escapes)
`
  'zip.u16le': `
Read a 2-byte little-endian unsigned integer
data: byte array to read from
off: start position (0-based)
v: the 2-byte little-endian unsigned integer (0 ~ 65535)
`
  'zip.u32le': `
Read a 4-byte little-endian unsigned integer
data: ZIP file byte array
off: start position (0-based)
v: the 4-byte little-endian unsigned integer (0 ~ 2^32-1)
`
  'zip.zip-entry.compressed-size': `
Read the entry's compressed size
csz: compressed byte count
`
  'zip.zip-entry.extract': `
Extract the entry content (stored and deflate)
out: decompressed raw bytes (stored copied directly, deflate inflated automatically)
`
  'zip.zip-entry.method': `
Read the entry's compression method (0=stored, 8=deflate)
method: compression method (0=stored, 8=deflate)
`
  'zip.zip-entry.name': `
Read the entry's file name
name: this entry's file name
`
  'zip.zip-entry.size': `
Read the entry's original size
sz: original byte count before compression
`
  'zip.zip-writer.add-dir': `
Add a directory entry
name: directory name (a trailing / is appended automatically when missing)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.add-file': `
Add a file to the archive (CRC32 computed automatically)
name: path name stored inside the archive
content: file content (stored verbatim with the stored method; CRC32 computed automatically)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.cd-put': `
Append one byte to cd-data
b: byte value to append (low 8 bits written to the central directory buffer)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.cd-write-u16': `
Write a 2-byte little-endian integer to the central directory
v: integer to write (low 16 bits appended little-endian to the central directory buffer)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.cd-write-u32': `
Write a 4-byte little-endian integer to the central directory
v: integer to write (low 32 bits appended little-endian to the central directory buffer)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.finalize': `
Write the central directory and EOCD, returning the complete archive data
out: complete ZIP archive bytes (local data + central directory + EOCD)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.put': `
Append one byte to data (push via a local variable)
b: byte value to append (low 8 bits written to the local data area)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.write-cd-entry': `
Write a central directory entry
name: file name
offset: starting offset of the entry's local file header
size: size before compression
compressed-size: size after compression
crc: CRC32 checksum of the content
`
  'zip.zip-writer.write-eocd': `
Write the End of Central Directory record
cd-offset: starting offset of the central directory
cd-size: total bytes of the central directory
`
  'zip.zip-writer.write-local-file': `
Write the local file header and content
name: file name (written into the header and data area)
content: file content (uncompressed, written verbatim as stored)
crc: CRC32 checksum of the content
`
  'zip.zip-writer.write-u16': `
Write a 2-byte little-endian integer
v: integer to write (low 16 bits appended little-endian)
`
  'zip.zip-writer.write-u32': `
Write a 4-byte little-endian integer
v: integer to write (low 32 bits appended little-endian)
`
  'zip.zip.compressed-size': `
Compressed size
idx: entry ordinal
csz: compressed byte count (same as the original when stored)
`
  'zip.zip.count': `
Return the number of entries in the ZIP
count: total entries (0 when the archive is corrupt)
`
  'zip.zip.entry': `
Get the idx-th entry
idx: entry ordinal
e: zip-entry handle bound to the entry's offset (fields read via its methods)
`
  'zip.zip.entry-off': `
Offset of the idx-th central directory entry
idx: entry ordinal (0 ~ total-1)
off: absolute offset of that central directory entry within the file data
`
  'zip.zip.extract': `
Extract the idx-th entry's content (stored and deflate)
idx: entry ordinal
out: decompressed raw bytes (stored copied directly, deflate inflated automatically)
`
  'zip.zip.find-eocd': `
Search backward from the end for the EOCD signature
off: offset of the EOCD signature (-1 when not found)
`
  'zip.zip.get-cd-off': `
Read the central directory offset (single return value, avoiding a multi-value compiler bug)
cd-off: starting offset of the central directory (0 when there is no EOCD)
`
  'zip.zip.get-total': `
Read the entry count (single return value)
total: total entries in the archive (0 when there is no EOCD)
`
  'zip.zip.method': `
Compression method (0=stored, 8=deflate)
idx: entry ordinal
method: compression method (0=stored uncompressed, 8=deflate)
`
  'zip.zip.name': `
File name of the idx-th entry
idx: entry ordinal
name: file name (may contain a / separated relative path)
`
  'zip.zip.size': `
Original size
idx: entry ordinal
sz: original byte count before compression
`
  'zlib.adler-32': `
Compute the Adler-32 checksum
data: input data ([]byte)
n: number of bytes actually included in the computation (i64)
returns sum: 32-bit checksum (i64), b in the high half and a in the low half, comparable with RFC 1950 implementations
`
  'zlib.zlib-compress': `
Build a zlib stream using stored blocks (BTYPE=00):
- 2-byte zlib header (78 9c)
- DEFLATE stored blocks (at most 65535 bytes each)
- 4-byte big-endian Adler-32 checksum
out []byte: complete zlib stream (2-byte header + stored blocks + 4-byte Adler-32)
`
  'zlib.zlib-consumed-stored': `
Compute the bytes consumed by a stored-block zlib stream
data: zlib stream starting at offset 0 ([]byte)
returns consumed: total bytes consumed (including header and Adler-32), 0 when a block is not stored
Accumulates per block: 5-byte block header + data length + 4-byte checksum, stopping at BFINAL or a non-stored block
`
  'zlib.zlib-decompress': `
Supports all DEFLATE block types (stored, fixed Huffman, dynamic Huffman)
Decompresses through gzip.inflate-decompress.
Tries the stored-block scan first (fast path), falling back to inflate on failure.
out ?[]byte: decompressed data (ok); nil when shorter than 6 bytes, header invalid, or decompression fails
`
  'zlib.zlib-decompress-stored': `
Decompress only stored-block zlib streams
data: zlib stream containing only BTYPE=00 blocks ([]byte)
returns out ?[]byte: decompressed data (some); nil for non-stored blocks or on failure
out ?[]byte: bytes decoded from BTYPE=00 blocks only; nil as soon as another block type or a mismatched end appears
`
  'zstd.bits-for-count': `
Compute the number of bits needed for count
count > 0: returns the significant-bit count of count (floor(log2(count)) + 1)
count <= 0: returns 0
count: frequency of a symbol in the normalized FSE table
n: minimum bits required for count (callers use tableLog - n to get the extra bits of that state)
`
  'zstd.fse-table.build': `
Build the FSE table from normalized counts
norm-count: normalized count of each symbol
max-symbol: maximum symbol value
table-log: log2 of the table size
`
  'zstd.fse-table.decode': `
Decode one FSE symbol
returns the symbol and the new state
br: bit reader used to fetch the extra bits for the state's transition to the next generation
state: current FSE decoding state (row index into the symbol table)
sym: symbol corresponding to the current state
new-state: state after transitioning to the next generation (next-state[state] plus the extra bits read)
`
  'zstd.zs-bit-reader.align-to-byte': 'Align to the next byte boundary'
  'zstd.zs-bit-reader.read-bit': `
Read one bit (LSB-first)
bit: the bit read (0 or 1); 0 when the data is exhausted
`
  'zstd.zs-bit-reader.read-bits': `
Read n bits (LSB-first)
n: number of bits to read (assembled into the integer LSB first, bit by bit)
v: integer assembled from the n bits read
`
  'zstd.zs-bit-reader.read-varint': `
Read a variable-length integer (LSB-first, 7 bits per group)
v: decoded integer value (low 7 bits of each byte significant, high bit 1 means more bytes follow)
`
  'zstd.zs-frame.decode-block': `
Decode one block (returns last-block ?bool: some = success carrying whether it is the final block, nil = failure)
last-block: tri-state result — ok(true) final block, ok(false) intermediate block both decoded successfully; nil means a truncated block header or a reserved block type
`
  'zstd.zs-frame.decode-compressed-block': `
Decode a compressed block
block-size: compressed block size
ok: true when the compressed block's literals and sequences sections parse and expand successfully (decoded bytes appended to out)
`
  'zstd.zs-frame.read-frame-header': `
Read the frame header
ok: true when the magic number validates and the header fields parse completely (pos then advanced to the first block's start)
`
  'zstd.zs-huffman.build': `
Build the Huffman decoding table
lengths: Huffman code length table per symbol (lengths determine the code distribution weights)
max-symbol: upper bound of symbol values (end of the lengths traversal; 255 for zstd byte symbols)
`
  'zstd.zs-huffman.decode': `
Decode one symbol
br: bit reader supplying the code bits (the codeword assembled bit by bit from the MSB end)
sym: decoded symbol value; 0 when no code matches within the maximum code length
`
  'zstd.zstd-compress': `
Compress data in zstd format (basic implementation)
data: raw data ([]byte)
out: zstd-compressed data ([]byte)
Note: currently a basic implementation using raw blocks;
full FSE + Huffman + LZ77 compression is left for a later implementation.
`
  'zstd.zstd-decompress': `
Decompress data in Zstandard format
data: zstd compressed data ([]byte)
out: decompressed data ([]byte)
`
}
